:: Xavier Collections Quest 1 [nobr]

/* Intro */
You are walking towards the bus where many of the other boys have gathered to catch a ride home <span style="color:Yellow">when you suddenly feel a hand on your shoulder and jump.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$XavierNickname</span>. Got a moment?”</span> You turn to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> standing behind you, surprisingly without his normal horde of followers. Though it doesn’t take long for you to spy them in the distance, a few of them giving you dirty looks as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>’s attention seems to be on you. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry to bother you, but I was wondering if you would help me with something?”</span> You ask what and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> motions for you to follow him, <span style="color:Yellow">seemingly taking that as you agreeing.</span>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                    },
                },
                    {
                    Name: "Xavier",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Uniform",
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                        },
                    },
                ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I have a… friend. He borrowed something from me the other day. It’s been a while, so I would like it back. 

<<if $Strength > 6>>
    I don’t expect any trouble, but seeing as you’re pretty strong, I figured it may be good to bring you along. 
<<elseif $Dexterity > 6>>
    I don’t expect any trouble, but seeing as you’re pretty quick on your feet, I figured it may be good to bring you along. 
<<elseif $Endurance > 6>>
    I don’t expect any trouble, but seeing as you’re pretty tough, I figured it may be good to bring you along. 
<<elseif $Smarts > 6>>
    I don’t expect any trouble, but seeing as you’re pretty clever, I figured it may be good to bring you along. 
<<elseif $Charm > 6>>
    I don’t expect any trouble, but seeing as you’re pretty good with words, I figured it may be good to bring you along. 
<<else>>
    I don’t expect any trouble, but I’d like the company. The others can be a bit much, and this is a delicate matter. 
<</if>>
Plus, you’re still new here. Maybe it would give me a chance to show you around. You know, just us?”</span> He gives you a smile, putting his arm around your shoulders and leading you into town. <span style="color:Yellow">Guess you’ll be joining <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> on whatever this collection errand is.</span> <br>
<br>
He keeps his word and takes the time to show you around town as you walk. Passing by the arcade and park, he points out various little things here and there. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The swing on the right is the best. The middle one leans to one side and the one on the left makes this annoying squeaking noise.”</span> He explains as you pass the playground, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You know, I used to love spending the afternoons there. The cool breeze and quiet was nice. Though, this was before I got half a dozen shadows that follow me everywhere.”</span> He chuckles, reminiscing.

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
                {
                Name: "Xavier",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

As you pass by the mall, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> stops and raises and eyebrow with a curious expression, grabbing you by the arm suddenly. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“One second. I want to show you something, follow me.”</span> He leads you towards one of the buildings outside of the mall, towards the back and far out of the way of the rest. The building he leads you to seems to be an old bookstore, with a few elders and young woman standing inside browsing the shelves. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> smiles at the sight, crossing his arms and looking up at the sign. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Up until a couple years ago, this place was a game store. You’d find all sorts of board games and card games and, well, any sort of games that weren’t electronic.”</span> He points out the faded paint on the walls where the old signs and posters used to be. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I was quite the addict in my youth. I used to come here every weekend. Even wore this ridiculous hat and sunglasses combo once I started to get hangers-on.”</span> He chuckles, shaking his head. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alas, they moved deeper into downtown to save money. Bit too much of a trip and it lost its appeal.”</span> <br>
<br>
Curious, you ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> why it lost its appeal and if he still plays those games. If he really liked them, why did he stop? He is just too busy or-? In response <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> turns to you, glaring with a smirk. He looks you up and down before tilting his head. You feel more than a little nervous, <span style="color:Yellow">wondering if you upset him or hit a nerve.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Here.”</span> Suddenly, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> takes off his backpack and tosses it at you. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Could you carry this for me, my shoulder’s a bit sore and it suits you better anyway. We should be there in just a minute.”</span> He turns on his heel slightly to continue walking. <br>
<br>
<div id="choice">
	<<link "Carry his backpack for him<br>">>
	<<replace "#choice">>
        Though it’s a bit of a struggle to carry both his and your own backpack, you manage to get the strap over your shoulder and follow behind <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>. Though you get the feeling both of your shoulders might be sore by the time you get there. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>, seeing you struggle, sighs and shakes his head. <br>
        
