Outside the trailer is a boy who looks to be about 2-3 years older than you messing with a beat-up car parked out front. Playing nearby in the yard is a young boy about your little brother’s age who happily swings a stick around without any shoes or a shirt on. Upon seeing you, or more accurately <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>, the older boy’s eyes go wide and he quickly rushes over to his brother, ordering him inside. The young boy looks at you both nervously, whispering something to his brother, before he is sent inside. <span style="color:Yellow">You get a bit worried about how fearful the older boy looks.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He- hey, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>…”</span> He swallows, walking over with a nervous expression, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I, uh… I didn’t think I’d see you around here. H- how are you doing?”</span> The boy stutters and moves to shake <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>’s hand before pulling it away awkwardly. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> seems to let him stew in his fear for a moment before speaking up. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey there, friend.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> sounds nice but with an undertone that worries you, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I believe you know what day it is? I hadn’t heard from you, so figured I’m come make sure everything is going as we discussed.”</span> The boy glances at you nervously, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> quickly gets his attention back. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He’s not the one talking to you, I am. It’s rather rude to ignore me.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I- I- I didn’t mean to… I mean, I- I don’t…”</span> The boy gulps once more, shaking slightly. He seems pretty afraid. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The shop hasn’t gotten payroll through yet, something with the computers. They assured me it’d be in tomorrow! I- I was going to come by as soon as it went in and-”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s all well and good, but last I checked I already gave you an extension.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> says, <span style="color:Yellow">still sounding creepily friendly,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“After that OTHER little issue you had. Really wearing down my trust here with all these little problems.”</span> <span style="color:Yellow">You start to feel nervous yourself, a thick tension building as this goes on. The older kid looks absolutely terrified as if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> is some loan shark in a movie who is going to pull a knife or something on him. Though you’re pretty sure <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> wouldn’t do something like that… right?</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I- I promise I’ll get it to you as soon as I can! Please, if I had it, I’d give it to you. It’s not my fault, I-”</span> The boy pleads, but is interrupted as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>, sighing loudly, holds up his hand. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Fine, fine.”</span> He waves his hand, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’re lucky I’m in such a good mood with my friend here. Suppose I can overlook it this time, as long as I see it tomorrow.”</span> The boy sighs in relief, thanking <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> until he is interrupted once more, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Though there is the problem of trust. I feel it may be close to breaking and while I can deal with someone I can trust, I’ll need some sort of assurance that I can still trust you. Something to show me you really are sorry about breaking it.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“O- of course! Anything!”</span> The boy replies worriedly, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I am so, so sorry! This won’t happen again I pro-”</span>

