<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$XavierNickname</span>?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> turns to you, not even bothering to let the kid finish, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’re my friend, so you understand what my trust is worth. What would you like him to do, to show us he can be trusted? Hm?”</span> He asks as the boy looks at you worriedly. <span style="color:Yellow">You hold your hands up, not feeling completely comfortable getting involved in this.</span> You have no part of this and- <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Come now, you must have some idea. Something to humble him, show us he really cares about this friendship.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> pauses for a moment, but you still don’t know if you want to get involved. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, if you don’t suggest something that can repair this breech, then I guess there is no way.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> shrugs as the boy begins to plead with you. <br>
